    "DifferentialDiagnosis": "Gorlin_Syndrome is unlikely due to the inflammatory/ulcerative nature and location on the tongue; it typically involves basal cell carcinomas elsewhere. Blue_Rubber_Bleb_Nevus_Syndrome is unlikely as the lesion morphology (erythematous plaque/ulcer) does not match the characteristic blue rubber bleb nevus (blue papules).",
    "PrimaryDiagnosis": "Behcet_Disease",
